# OpenSpec phase gate (implementation)

When an **active** OpenSpec change under `openspec/changes/<name>/` (exclude `archive/`) has **`ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md`**, agents **must** complete the phase architecture gate **in the session transcript** before any firmware edit for that change.

**Does not replace** [architecture-checkpoint-bugfix](architecture-checkpoint-bugfix.mdc) — both apply on stop-path / capture-commit work.

Authority: [`docs/Authority/DELIVERY_RULES.md`](docs/Authority/DELIVERY_RULES.md) § OpenSpec phase gate.

---

## Mandatory load order (before firmware)

1. [`docs/Runtime/CURRENT_WORK.md`](docs/Runtime/CURRENT_WORK.md) — confirm active change and phase
2. `openspec/changes/<name>/ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md` — **§ Per-phase gates** for target phase
3. `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md` — only unchecked items for **this phase**
4. `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md` — when phase touches ownership or transitions

If `ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md` is missing for an active change that touches ownership or stop-path behavior, **stop** and propose adding the review artifact (or run `/opsx:explore`) before coding.

---

## Architecture gate (post in chat before first edit)

Copy the phase's **Architecture gate** table from `ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md` and answer explicitly:

| Question | Required |
|----------|----------|
| **Owner module** | Which class/function owns this phase's behavior |
| **Primary invariant** | One sentence from ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW north star or design |
| **Ownership change?** | YES / NO — if YES without user-approved phase → **stop** (design session) |
| **State transition change?** | YES / NO — if YES without user-approved phase → **stop** |
| **Behavior-preserving?** | YES / NO for this phase (Phases marked preserving must stay preserving) |
| **Reuse decision** | YES — extend `<owner>.<method>` OR NO — cite DEC-### + rationale |
| **Phase scope** | Phase N only — list files you will touch |

Also answer the two [architecture-checkpoint](architecture-checkpoint-bugfix.mdc) questions when the edit touches capture stop, commit, persistence gating, or deferred FSM paths.

**Do not** edit firmware until this block is posted (unless user explicitly requests investigation-only / read-only).

---

## Protected paths (extra scrutiny)

Any edit under these areas requires the gate above **even for bugfixes**:

| Area | Examples |
|------|----------|
| Capture stop / commit | `Track::stopRecording`, `stopOverdubbing`, `queueOverdubStopCommit`, `processDeferredOverdubStop`, `commitCaptureForStop`, `finalizeCommitSideEffects` |
| Loop seal | `Loop::commitCapturePass`, `finalizeLoopAtStop` |
| Cancel / abort scatter | `cancelDeferredOverdubStop` and new `cancel*` / `abort*` on capture lifecycle |
| Slot capture stop | `handleToggleRecordForSlot`, `finalizeCaptureAndSelectSlot` |
| Persistence gating | `StorageManager` deferred save / recovery paths tied to capture stop |
| Post-commit projection | `resetPlaybackState`, `projectionCycleStartTick`, `ensurePlaybackWindowBuilt`, display snapshot after stop |

Read [`docs/Guides/LOOP_MIDI_STORAGE_AND_VALIDATION.md`](docs/Guides/LOOP_MIDI_STORAGE_AND_VALIDATION.md) before changing stop or commit paths.

---

## Forbidden without approved phase / design

| Pattern | Why blocked |
|---------|-------------|
| New `cancel*` / `abort*` at **new** call sites | Symptom patch — route through lifecycle owner (`resetCaptureCommitSession` / Phase 4 design) |
| Same post-stop side effect in **two** stop paths | Violates single commit owner — use shared pipeline / post-commit hook |
| New `*Helper` / free function on stop path | Extend existing owner unless DECISION_REVIEW reuse = NO |
| New top-level Manager or parallel FSM | Formal trigger — reassessment + DECISION_LOG |
| Phase marked behavior-preserving but changes scheduling, telemetry contract, or HITL pass criteria | Phase violation — split to later phase or get user approval |
| Checking off `tasks.md` phase without **Implementation review** | Gate incomplete |

Extending an **existing** method on the documented owner for the **current phase scope** is allowed after the gate passes.

---

## Implementation review (before merge / phase checkoff)

Before marking phase tasks done in `tasks.md`, complete the phase **Implementation review** checklist in `ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md` and use [`docs/Agents/reviewer.md`](docs/Agents/reviewer.md) output format.

Builder sessions must include:

```markdown
## Architecture gate (Phase N)
- Owner: ...
- Invariant: ...
- Ownership change: NO | YES (approved Phase N)
- Transition change: NO | YES (approved Phase N)
- Reuse: YES — extend ... | NO — DEC-###

## Tests
- [ ] pio test -e native
- [ ] Phase HITL gate (if ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW requires)
```

---

## Session scope

- **One OpenSpec phase per session** unless user explicitly approves multiple phases.
- Do not mix active changes (e.g. DEC-023 Phase 1 + DEC-020 Phase 5) in one implementation pass without user confirmation.
- Symptom fixes outside the active phase → investigate and report; do not patch unless user approves scope expansion or a dedicated bugfix with checkpoint both **no**.

---

## When ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md does not exist

- **Trivial bugfix** on unrelated paths: [architecture-checkpoint](architecture-checkpoint-bugfix.mdc) only.
- **Non-trivial** or stop-path work on a change without review doc: add `ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md` (Phase 0 doc-only) or `/opsx:propose` before firmware.
